eft" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134017252.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At just eleven years old, Mateo Castillo-Bonde has already made a significant impact, mesmerizing audiences with his guitar skills. His stunning solo at the State Fair, where he shared the stage with iconic producers Jimmy Jam and Terry Lewis, showcased his remarkable talent. After only three years of dedicated practice, sparked by a museum visit, Mateo continues to encourage others to explore their creative passions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-mateo-castillo-bonde-the-11-year-old-minneapolis-guitarist-who-went-from-playing-in-his-bedroom-to-performing-before-thousands-with-jimmy-jam-and-terry-lewis/articleshow/134017252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-mateo-castillo-bonde-the-11-year-old-minneapolis-guitarist-who-went-from-playing-in-his-bedroom-to-performing-before-thousands-with-jimmy-jam-and-terry-lewis/articleshow/134017252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T21:03:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134017512,imgsize-105334.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota trees adapted to 3.4°C warming, cutting expected CO₂ rise by 80%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133971140.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/scientists-warmed-minnesota-forest-trees-by-3-4c-for-years-expecting-respiration-to-surge-23-the-trees-adapted-and-erased-nearly-80-of-that-increase/articleshow/133971140.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/scientists-warmed-minnesota-forest-trees-by-3-4c-for-years-expecting-respiration-to-surge-23-the-trees-adapted-and-erased-nearly-80-of-that-increase/articleshow/133971140.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T21:02:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133971337,imgsize-1813421.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Iran-backed Houthis seize key Red Sea port in blow to Saudi forces]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134015236.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-backed-houthis-seize-key-red-sea-port-in-blow-to-saudi-forces/articleshow/134015236.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-backed-houthis-seize-key-red-sea-port-in-blow-to-saudi-forces/articleshow/134015236.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T20:49:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134017353,imgsize-115441.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US resumes immigrant visa processing for Hungary, Poland while wider pause continues: What it means]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134016220.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-resumes-immigrant-visa-processing-for-hungary-poland-while-wider-pause-continues-what-it-means/articleshow/134016220.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-resumes-immigrant-visa-processing-for-hungary-poland-while-wider-pause-continues-what-it-means/articleshow/134016220.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T20:36:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134016488,imgsize-42784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hong Kong cattle DNA reveals how livestock adapted to island life]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133997784.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/cattle-were-left-behind-in-hong-kong-centuries-ago-a-2026-genome-study-found-their-dna-holds-a-record-of-how-livestock-adapted-to-island-life/articleshow/133997784.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/cattle-were-left-behind-in-hong-kong-centuries-ago-a-2026-genome-study-found-their-dna-holds-a-record-of-how-livestock-adapted-to-island-life/articleshow/133997784.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T14:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133997784,imgsize-174685.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The US had just two 500-foot smokestacks in 1970 and more than 180 by 1985 to dilute pollution]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134014938.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an effort to mitigate local air pollution, American power companies constructed towering smokestacks, effectively releasing sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides into higher winds. Unfortunately, this practice contributed to acid rain, harming ecosystems throughout North America. In response, Congress revised the Clean Air Act to restrict the use of tall stacks and improve emission control by emphasizing source capture instead.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-had-just-two-500-foot-smokestacks-in-1970-and-more-than-180-by-1985-to-dilute-local-pollution-the-taller-stacks-sent-emissions-farther-downwind-and-helped-spread-acid-rain/articleshow/134014938.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-had-just-two-500-foot-smokestacks-in-1970-and-more-than-180-by-1985-to-dilute-local-pollution-the-taller-stacks-sent-emissions-farther-downwind-and-helped-spread-acid-rain/articleshow/134014938.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:59:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134015120,imgsize-46957.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Jersey built a massive seawall to protect a highway and beach houses from erosion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134014563.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In New Jersey, the construction of a seawall has safeguarded properties but has inadvertently resulted in the disappearance of the sandy shoreline. The energy from waves is redirected downwards, which has stripped away sand and left no beach visible even during low tide. This hard engineering tactic disrupts the natural flow of sand and hinders the migration of barrier islands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-jersey-built-a-massive-seawall-to-protect-a-highway-and-beach-houses-from-erosion-usgs-says-the-wall-concentrated-wave-energy-until-the-beach-it-was-meant-to-defend-disappeared-completely/articleshow/134014563.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-jersey-built-a-massive-seawall-to-protect-a-highway-and-beach-houses-from-erosion-usgs-says-the-wall-concentrated-wave-energy-until-the-beach-it-was-meant-to-defend-disappeared-completely/articleshow/134014563.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:52:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134014806,imgsize-160554.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gwyneth Paltrow turned $4.9 million Montecito property into 14,000-sq-ft estate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134014011.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Gwyneth Paltrow bought about 2.4 acres in Montecito for $4.9 million in 2016, razed the existing structures and embarked on a ground-up project that took about six years. The result was a roughly 14,000-square-foot home powered by solar energy and equipped with a graywater system.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2016-gwyneth-paltrow-bought-2-4-acres-in-montecito-for-4-9-million-during-a-historic-drought-over-a-6-year-journey-she-razed-two-old-homes-and-built-a-14000-sq-ft-estate-with-more-than-60-solar-panels-and-a-graywater-system/articleshow/134014011.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2016-gwyneth-paltrow-bought-2-4-acres-in-montecito-for-4-9-million-during-a-historic-drought-over-a-6-year-journey-she-razed-two-old-homes-and-built-a-14000-sq-ft-estate-with-more-than-60-solar-panels-and-a-graywater-system/articleshow/134014011.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:44:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134014056,imgsize-129499.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New York investigator accused of tracking ex-girlfriend 3,000 times using Flock cameras; suspended after 4,000 searches]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-york-investigator-accused-of-tracking-ex-girlfriend-3000-times-using-flock-cameras-suspended-after-4000-searches/articleshow/134014253.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-york-investigator-accused-of-tracking-ex-girlfriend-3000-times-using-flock-cameras-suspended-after-4000-searches/articleshow/134014253.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:44:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134014463,imgsize-27082.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The US built nearly 2,000 km of Mississippi River levees; helping erase 4,900 sq km of coastal land]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134013976.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The construction of levees along the Mississippi River has led to significant coastal land erosion in Louisiana by obstructing critical river sediment from reaching coastal estuaries. In an effort to combat this issue, environmental agencies are now reintroducing river mud into the affected bayous. This initiative is focused on rejuvenating the coastline and revitalizing marshland ecosystems, serving as a potential blueprint for delta restoration throughout southern Louisiana.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-built-nearly-2000-km-of-mississippi-river-levees-to-control-floods-the-barriers-cut-sediment-off-from-louisiana-wetlands-helping-erase-about-4900-sq-km-of-coastal-land/articleshow/134013976.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-us-built-nearly-2000-km-of-mississippi-river-levees-to-control-floods-the-barriers-cut-sediment-off-from-louisiana-wetlands-helping-erase-about-4900-sq-km-of-coastal-land/articleshow/134013976.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:40:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134014185,imgsize-185524.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Britain brought back wild bison after 6,000 years; their grazing could create new habitats]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134003319.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The historic return of wild bison to Britain, absent for 6,000 years, is made possible by the Blean Bison Project. This initiative not only aims to reinstate these creatures but also to rejuvenate the woodland ecosystem they inhabit. Through their natural grazing and movements, they are instrumental in creating diverse habitats that support biodiversity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/britain-brought-back-wild-bison-after-6000-years-their-grazing-could-reshape-forests-and-create-new-habitats-for-other-wildlife/articleshow/134003319.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/britain-brought-back-wild-bison-after-6000-years-their-grazing-could-reshape-forests-and-create-new-habitats-for-other-wildlife/articleshow/134003319.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134003480,imgsize-296289.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Two beavers were unexpectedly released in Cornwall; they have built a dam six months later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134002697.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Two beavers have unexpectedly settled at Helman Tor nature reserve. Their dam building and feeding activities are creating a more varied habitat. The new pools and altered water flow are attracting other wildlife species. Cornwall Wildlife Trust is monitoring the pair while planning wider reintroductions. This unexpected arrival supports the trust's long-term conservation goals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/two-beavers-were-unexpectedly-released-in-cornwall-six-months-later-they-have-built-a-dam-that-is-reshaping-the-landscape-and-attracting-wildlife/articleshow/134002697.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/two-beavers-were-unexpectedly-released-in-cornwall-six-months-later-they-have-built-a-dam-that-is-reshaping-the-landscape-and-attracting-wildlife/articleshow/134002697.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134002987,imgsize-269555.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Denmark and Germany turn Bornholm into a 3GW offshore Island wind hub]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134002360.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/denmark-and-germany-are-turning-an-island-into-a-giant-offshore-power-hub-3gw-of-wind-energy-will-flow-to-two-countries/articleshow/134002360.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/denmark-and-germany-are-turning-an-island-into-a-giant-offshore-power-hub-3gw-of-wind-energy-will-flow-to-two-countries/articleshow/134002360.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134002360,imgsize-112654.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Can Iran hurt Trump at ballot box? Tehran’s new war strategy explained]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134012454.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/can-iran-hurt-trump-at-ballot-box-tehrans-new-war-strategy-explained/articleshow/134012454.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/can-iran-hurt-trump-at-ballot-box-tehrans-new-war-strategy-explained/articleshow/134012454.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:05:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134012642,imgsize-64036.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Golden Gate University sells SF campus for $31.6 million; a 46-storey tower is proposed in its place]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134004642.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Golden Gate University has sold its longtime downtown San Francisco campus for $31.6 million after more than 170 years in the city. The seven-storey property could be demolished to make way for a proposed 46-storey tower, with developers considering either a 700-foot office building or a mixed-use project with offices and homes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-operating-in-san-francisco-for-more-than-170-years-golden-gate-university-sold-its-236680-sq-ft-downtown-campus-for-31-6-million-a-46-story-700-foot-tower-is-proposed-in-its-place/articleshow/134004642.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-operating-in-san-francisco-for-more-than-170-years-golden-gate-university-sold-its-236680-sq-ft-downtown-campus-for-31-6-million-a-46-story-700-foot-tower-is-proposed-in-its-place/articleshow/134004642.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="ht